# 🎬 Movies Metadata Analysis — NTI Final Project

Cleaning, analysis, and interactive dashboarding of a 45K+ movie dataset (TMDB Movies Metadata), built as the final project for the NTI Data Analysis track.

## 📌 Overview

This project turns a large, messy movie catalogue into a reliable analytics asset and answers real business questions about profitability, genres, and audience ratings — then visualizes everything in an interactive Power BI dashboard.

**Dataset:** 45,346 movies · Release years 1888–2020 · Source: TMDB / Movies Metadata

## 📂 Project Structure

```
├── New analysis.py                     # Main data cleaning & transformation script
├── movies_metadata_cleaned (2).csv     # Intermediate cleaned file
├── movies_metadata_final.csv           # Final analysis-ready dataset
├── movies_metadata_final.xlsx          # Final dataset (Excel format)
├── Project.pbix                        # Power BI dashboard
└── Data_Analysis_Project_NTI.docx      # Full project report
```

## 🧹 Data Cleaning

The cleaning script (`New analysis.py`) runs in 10 stages:

1. Remove duplicate records (by movie id)
2. Parse and validate release dates
3. Normalize text fields (strip whitespace, standardize case)
4. Fill missing text fields with defaults
5. Fix invalid numeric values (negative budget/revenue/votes)
6. Add derived columns: `profit` and `roi`
7. Remove impossible values (e.g. runtime ≤ 0, rating outside 0–10)
8. Drop unusable rows (missing title/date)
9. Cast columns to proper data types
10. Export final dataset

**Result:** 0 missing release dates, 0 false-zero runtimes, correctly typed columns.

## 📊 Business Questions Answered

- How has production volume changed over time?
- Which genres dominate the catalogue?
- Does a bigger budget guarantee a bigger return?
- Which genres return the most profit per film?
- What are the highest-grossing and highest-ROI titles?
- Do audiences reward the same films the box office does?

## 📈 Dashboard (Power BI)

Single-page interactive report with:
- KPI cards — Total Profit, Average ROI, Total Revenue
- Profit trend by release year
- Profit share by genre (donut chart)
- Audience rating by genre (bar chart)
- Top-rated titles
- Slicers for year and release status
